{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1182493-lancea-sanctum-and-evilness","id":1182493,"title":"Lancea Sanctum and 'evilness'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-04T21:09:49-08:00","id":1182493,"title":"Lancea Sanctum and 'evilness'","content":"Today I was having intruging dream. It was High Middle Ages, somewhere in Europe. I was LS Priest, probably Ventrue. I found Christian cathedra, full of mortals, preying at night. Suddenly, I come forth and accused mortal priest - maybe a bishop? - that he's ways of running community was 'truly evil'. He did not believe me and said to go away. When I refused, he threatened me with weapon and violence. I did not bow, simply going forward, on the steps of alter. He took some weapon and call on his guards - but could not killed me as I was Kindred. Then he screamed as I sucked his life of him on the alter, taking this church in control. And then I woke up.<br /> <br /> Question is simple -<b> How much this king scenario is possible in VtR setting? Can Lancea Sanctum accuse mortals of 'evil' or 'wickedness' and punish them from their norms?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-05-2018, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T00:56:30-08:00","id":1182519,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the question of whether a Sanctified would do take over a mortal congregation instead of guiding the Damned, would a Kindred ever do something so blatant in front of mortals?<br /> <br /> I can see a vampire scaring the priest with Nightmare or commanding him to step down with Dominate, and then perhaps charming everyone else with Majesty. Or using just Majesty for everything. But not something like openly drinking someone to death, even if it\u2019s the Middle Ages. Maybe yes if the church was an isolated, closed, small community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T03:25:07-08:00","id":1182531,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand the Sanctified that is basically their schtick; they test the faith of mortal believers. Having said that, I don't think they'd openly call out a priest who is evil. Their tactic, in general, would be to lead the priest astray, to try and tempt him into doing evil. If he fails the test, if he fails God, then they'd gut him. But probably not in front of the parish. Although, if the entire church community is on the edge of herecy, a zealous Sanctified might take the gamble of breaking the Masquerade to make an example out of their wayward priest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T05:30:00-08:00","id":1182556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1182493-lancea-sanctum-and-evilness?p=1182531#post1182531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand the Sanctified that is basically their schtick; they test the faith of mortal believers. Having said that, I don't think they'd openly call out a priest who is evil. Their tactic, in general, would be to lead the priest astray, to try and tempt him into doing evil. If he fails the test, if he fails God, then they'd gut him. But probably not in front of the parish. Although, if the entire church community is on the edge of herecy, a zealous Sanctified might take the gamble of breaking the Masquerade to make an example out of their wayward priest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can kind of see it going like that, as a blatant masquerade breach/display of the supernatural might be interpretated as a &quot;dark miracle/intervention of the divine&quot;, what while unusual, still fits with the Lancea Sanctum's ethos to a tee. That said such a kindred would certainly try to play it out in a way to not only test the priest's worthiness but drive home to the flock they are seeing the hand of the Lord's hand at work, as either the devil taking it's due or an avenging angel (of sorts) bringing the due punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-05-2018, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T11:49:30-08:00","id":1183001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1182493-lancea-sanctum-and-evilness#post1182493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Christian cathedral, full of mortals, <b>preying</b> at night.[/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a typo, but to me this sounds like a very evocative plot hook <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T01:02:29-08:00","id":1183194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1182493-lancea-sanctum-and-evilness#post1182493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today I was having intruging dream. It was High Middle Ages, somewhere in Europe. I was LS Priest, probably Ventrue. I found Christian cathedra, full of mortals, preying at night. Suddenly, I come forth and accused mortal priest - maybe a bishop? - that he's ways of running community was 'truly evil'. He did not believe me and said to go away. When I refused, he threatened me with weapon and violence. I did not bow, simply going forward, on the steps of alter. He took some weapon and call on his guards - but could not killed me as I was Kindred. Then he screamed as I sucked his life of him on the alter, taking this church in control. And then I woke up.<br /> <br /> Question is simple -<b> How much this king scenario is possible in VtR setting? Can Lancea Sanctum accuse mortals of 'evil' or 'wickedness' and punish them from their norms?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it fits the Lancea perfectly!<br /> <br /> I've always seen the Undead Church as similar to real-life religion; they have come up with a way of explaining their &quot;place&quot; in the world. That &quot;God&quot; has a plan for them.<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators, and predators feed on prey. Humans are their prey, so its only natural they feed on them (its nature - its as God planned it to be).<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum &quot;churches&quot; are herds of humans who are likely unaware of their &quot;priest&quot; being undead. They accept the preaching of how many is superior to beast, and how the superior feed on those below not out of greed - but necessity (ignorantly aware they are giving permision to the priest to eat them later - it would be hypocritical to protest to this; and even sinful to be greedy that man can eat meat, but in turn cannot be eaten).<br /> <br /> As to YOUR dream and idea though - it still works. Vampires are Predators, but are intellegent Predators. They can be selective of prey, just like a wolf or cat targets the weakest of animals to eat. In the case of the vampires of the cloth, I look at them like Hannibal Lectre - he CAN (and does) kill without hesitation, but he recycles the meat (eats it). MORE so, he often kills humans to make the race better (I remember he killed and ate a person in a orchestra because their playing brought down the whole artistic power of the whole).<br /> <br /> Vampire Priests can do the same - seek out targets that are harming humanity, and take them down. Eat the sinners so the pure can live in saftey. They are the sheep dog's for the folk - save that THESE sheep dogs are x20 the size of any wolf that would prey on their lambs.<br /> <br /> Inevitably I think the Vampires of the Lancea Sanctum are seeking comfort - they want to believe their curse has purpose, and they obsess to believe in it.<br /> <br /> This CAN go to an extreme of a religious fanataic as well - but its how you play your character.<br /> <br /> All in all - your idea seems completely fine to accuse mortals for wickedness. Its all perspective. What is illegal in one country (or even in one time) may be legal now. What if a Vampire from Prohibition saw people drinking now? Maybe they'd forget how much time has past and kill the person having a casual beer because its wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T01:02:29-08:00","id":1183195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1182493-lancea-sanctum-and-evilness#post1182493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today I was having intruging dream. It was High Middle Ages, somewhere in Europe. I was LS Priest, probably Ventrue. I found Christian cathedra, full of mortals, preying at night. Suddenly, I come forth and accused mortal priest - maybe a bishop? - that he's ways of running community was 'truly evil'. He did not believe me and said to go away. When I refused, he threatened me with weapon and violence. I did not bow, simply going forward, on the steps of alter. He took some weapon and call on his guards - but could not killed me as I was Kindred. Then he screamed as I sucked his life of him on the alter, taking this church in control. And then I woke up.<br /> <br /> Question is simple -<b> How much this king scenario is possible in VtR setting? Can Lancea Sanctum accuse mortals of 'evil' or 'wickedness' and punish them from their norms?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it fits the Lancea perfectly!<br /> <br /> I've always seen the Undead Church as similar to real-life religion; they have come up with a way of explaining their &quot;place&quot; in the world. That &quot;God&quot; has a plan for them.<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators, and predators feed on prey. Humans are their prey, so its only natural they feed on them (its nature - its as God planned it to be).<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum &quot;churches&quot; are herds of humans who are likely unaware of their &quot;priest&quot; being undead. They accept the preaching of how many is superior to beast, and how the superior feed on those below not out of greed - but necessity (ignorantly aware they are giving permision to the priest to eat them later - it would be hypocritical to protest to this; and even sinful to be greedy that man can eat meat, but in turn cannot be eaten).<br /> <br /> As to YOUR dream and idea though - it still works. Vampires are Predators, but are intellegent Predators. They can be selective of prey, just like a wolf or cat targets the weakest of animals to eat. In the case of the vampires of the cloth, I look at them like Hannibal Lectre - he CAN (and does) kill without hesitation, but he recycles the meat (eats it). MORE so, he often kills humans to make the race better (I remember he killed and ate a person in a orchestra because their playing brought down the whole artistic power of the whole).<br /> <br /> Vampire Priests can do the same - seek out targets that are harming humanity, and take them down. Eat the sinners so the pure can live in saftey. They are the sheep dog's for the folk - save that THESE sheep dogs are x20 the size of any wolf that would prey on their lambs.<br /> <br /> Inevitably I think the Vampires of the Lancea Sanctum are seeking comfort - they want to believe their curse has purpose, and they obsess to believe in it.<br /> <br /> This CAN go to an extreme of a religious fanataic as well - but its how you play your character.<br /> <br /> All in all - your idea seems completely fine to accuse mortals for wickedness. Its all perspective. What is illegal in one country (or even in one time) may be legal now. What if a Vampire from Prohibition saw people drinking now? Maybe they'd forget how much time has past and kill the person having a casual beer because its wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:26:58-08:00","id":1185250,"title":"","content":"Leading mortals to temptation and punishing those who give in is standard practice for the Sanctified. The only thing about the described scenario that doesn't fit is doing it in front of the whole congregation, as LetS is very serious about upholding the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}